</table>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"d1b472429666" id=3D"CareerPilot=E2=80=93MVPPRD-Pilotboundar=
y">Pilot boundary</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5d539f80e2b3">The controlled pilot allows invitation-only ve=
rified headhunters to submit private JDs, receive opted-in high-fit profile=
s and request approved CV access. A private JD does not become a paid publi=
c job ad or a partner job feed. Broad self-service employer search, unverif=
ied recruiter access, bulk CV export, automated hiring decisions, auto-appl=
y/ATS submission and headhunter payments remain outside the pilot.</p>
<p local-id=3D"90b5044c6709">FR14=E2=80=99s full employer/recruiter trust i=
ndicator and CPA-77 / US13 remain post-MVP. The pilot must nevertheless pro=
vide basic recruiter verification, candidate report/block and controlled sh=
aring under FR25/FR30/NFR12 before any recruiter contact.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"507f6558bdfe" id=3D"CareerPilot=E2=80=93MVPPRD-10.Timeline"=
>10. Timeline</h2>
<p local-id=3D"cdca21192c13">Public launch is on <time datetime=3D"2027-06-=
14" class=3D"date-future">14 Jun 2027</time>, after 17 two-week sprints sta=
rting <time datetime=3D"2026-10-19" class=3D"date-future">19 Oct 2026</time=
>; sprint 18 is a stabilisation buffer before the fixed Q2 deadline. The te=
am is 2 engineers, 1 ML engineer and 1 PM. Sprint dates follow the 2-week c=
adence; the allocation of work to sprints is [ASSUMPTION]. Building starts =
once the core problem is understood: S1=E2=80=93S6 validate the problem and=
 design the solution, and the six build sprints in Jira (Sprint 1=E2=80=936=
) run as S7=E2=80=93S12.</p>
