<p local-id=3D"2236b71049b2">Additional next steps: PM confirms recruiter i=
nterview participants and pilot owners by 16 October 2026 [ASSUMPTION]; eng=
ineering reviews estimates and capacity at G2; define verification evidence=
, consent text, retention/deletion behaviour, seven-day freshness and shari=
ng expiry before pilot beta.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"35d9397fd15a" id=3D"CareerPilot=E2=80=93MVPPRD-11.OpenQuest=
ions">11. Open Questions</h2>
<p local-id=3D"1e11ca623f15">These must be answered before engineering revi=
ew.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fb48439e9560"><strong>Product and scope</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b52b9f544fc3">
<li local-id=3D"acdaa660f033">
<p local-id=3D"4d9c40dc54a1">Which payment provider runs the prepaid wallet=
 after launch?</p>
<p local-id=3D"159d8e185296"><strong>Answer: </strong>None: this is a class=
room exercise. PayPal or Revolut may appear as a mock-up for visual consist=
ency only.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a473fc290b29">
<p local-id=3D"0eb944c6b2d7">Is FR3 (multi-language CV merge) a Should, or =
a Must for the multilingual persona at launch?</p>
<p local-id=3D"17a865204ff6"><strong>Answer: </strong>Keep as Should. Typic=
al case: a keyword present in the German CV is missing from the English CV.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ebd805c1a97">
<p local-id=3D"75563faab25e">Which Should items (FR12, FR13, FR20, FR21) ar=
e cut first if G3 slips?</p>
<p local-id=3D"4f6aef942b2d"><strong>Answer: </strong>Prioritise by RICE (s=
ection 5). Cut order if G3 slips: FR21, then FR13 (kept as a demo screen); =
FR12 is cheap and stays; FR20 moves to Must because confidence replaces the=
 completeness gate.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"58a1e6b1acd0"><strong>Matching and scoring</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"5" local-id=3D"3c965345ea35">
<li local-id=3D"2b6bb3fb4d0b">
<p local-id=3D"7ba884ae90f5">What are the criteria weights in the score mod=
el, and who signs them off?</p>
<p local-id=3D"237c06f7a810"><strong>Answer: </strong>Documented in "Calcul=
ating the Matching score" (child page of this PRD).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"31005ec6e0ed">
<p local-id=3D"cf0ef4ff89eb">Which fields are mandatory and how are complet=
eness weights validated, now that completeness is no longer a gate?</p>
<p local-id=3D"32ef78131a38"><strong>Answer: </strong>Documented in "Calcul=
ating profile completeness" (child page of this PRD). Completeness is no lo=
nger a gate (FR18).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"482f339e38af">
<p local-id=3D"fcd92db0323f">What counts as a must-have requirement that ca=
ps the score, and by how much?</p>
<p local-id=3D"492452d50993"><strong>Answer: </strong>Documented in "Calcul=
ating the Matching score": an unmet must-have caps the score just below the=
 user's minimum fit, so the job leaves the main list but stays visible with=
 the reason named.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"779aba95022f">
<p local-id=3D"7905994b5168">Which labelled dataset and which accuracy thre=
shold prove the score at G1?</p>
<p local-id=3D"8aa4d2f18198"><strong>Answer: </strong>The demo illustrates =
the scoring approach; expert-labelled validation is planned.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"a88bad2d4b1c"><strong>Data, legal and trust</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"9" local-id=3D"b4011b93c2ee">
<li local-id=3D"bc6fc696d3bb">
<p local-id=3D"8274e011efd6">Is the coverage of the Bundesagentur f=C3=BCr =
Arbeit lists enough to launch, and which partner feeds come first with empl=
oyer login?</p>
<p local-id=3D"6a871ae2750a"><strong>Answer: </strong>For the student MVP/d=
emo, yes, provided clearly labelled mock job data is used where necessary t=
o demonstrate matching. For a commercial launch, BA coverage alone should n=
ot be assumed sufficient; evaluate it against target roles, locations, fres=
hness and relevant jobs per candidate. Prioritise employer-posted jobs once=
 employer login exists, then licensed or contracted partner feeds. The BA s=
upports employer job publication and an HR-BA-XML interface, but its public=
 API is not equivalent to a complete candidate-facing job feed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a875e40cc3b3">
<p local-id=3D"dba4b80c3373">Does the EU AI Act apply to the candidate-side=
 MVP, and what does it require?</p>
<p local-id=3D"c72477c50986"><strong>Answer: </strong>For the classroom pro=
totype, CareerPilot is a demonstration system, not a production recruitment=
 decision system. A real deployment needs specialist legal classification: =
AI for recruitment or selection, including analysing or filtering applicati=
ons and evaluating candidates, is in the AI Act's high-risk employment area=
, while a candidate-side assistant that only helps the individual understan=
d jobs may be classified differently depending on its intended purpose and =
whether its outputs influence employer decisions. Recruiter-side evaluation=
 makes the high-risk provisions particularly relevant; Annex III requiremen=
ts are scheduled to apply from 2 December 2027. The MVP still designs for t=
ransparency, human oversight, explainability, traceability, data quality, b=
ias monitoring, security and clear disclosure of AI use. See chapter 12.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"20c0d4d34a01">
<p local-id=3D"40aeed667712">How long do we keep CVs, generated documents a=
nd LLM logs, and how does deletion reach all of them?</p>
<p local-id=3D"ceed26e9dbf9"><strong>Answer: </strong>No real candidates ar=
e used in the demo, so no storage is required. For a real pilot, see chapte=
r 12.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e5f9133f081">
<p local-id=3D"6799d8c3fd28">Which signals define a "verified" employer or =
recruiter for FR14, once employer login exists?</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"1541832d730b"><strong>Metrics and launch</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"13" local-id=3D"20cf8704ce3e">
<li local-id=3D"54882bb412b7">
<p local-id=3D"c38f0de6bc80">How is "hired" captured as an exit reason so r=
etention excludes successful users?</p>
<p local-id=3D"80100e914979"><strong>Answer: </strong>Retention excludes hi=
red users; they count as success stories.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c1208508d2ce">
<p local-id=3D"f4343f1b7f0f">Who are the ~500 beta users in Germany, and ho=
w are they recruited?</p>
<p local-id=3D"d36ad4c02347"><strong>Answer: </strong>For a real pilot, rec=
ruit through social channels such as Facebook and LinkedIn.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"70c7b8756d1c">
<p local-id=3D"873009ba4bd8">Which metric targets in section 4 are launch b=
lockers at G4, and which are post-launch goals?</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"1be52d0458af" id=3D"CareerPilot=E2=80=93MVPPRD-Headhunterop=
enquestions">Headhunter open questions</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"532c281c-6716-4868-9742-07dcdb8a91b2">
<li local-id=3D"11585a81-45a2-487e-b36b-623b8ed75a56">
<p local-id=3D"2a2ce54940ee">Who approves the recruiter identity/organisati=
on verification process, how often is it rechecked, and who handles reports=
 and suspension?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f9514486-34fe-48fa-8564-f3c9a95c4606">
<p local-id=3D"1572ddf5f40d">Which profile fields may appear in the initial=
 pseudonymised preview, and what purpose, retention and recipient obligatio=
ns apply to approved CV access?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e234d94-f034-4aec-a269-c44e06197e05">
<p local-id=3D"90528a04df73">Is seven-day availability confirmation suffici=
ently fresh, how is =E2=80=9Ccan start now=E2=80=9D validated, and when sho=
uld reconfirmation reminders run?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e4c4db25-fd73-4630-a167-a6ef22c8ffc9">
<p local-id=3D"05875870f0a2">Confirm seven-day recruiter/JD-specific CV acc=
ess expiry; how do deletion, revocation, caches and already downloaded copi=
es interact?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"295d8599-be27-4e81-9f55-1da3fb20b213">
<p local-id=3D"8f3990f0c14b">Which high-confidence definition, must-have ca=
ps and expert-labelled dataset validate =E2=89=A590% fit without score infl=
ation or unfair exclusions?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f0252e1b-228a-4211-9320-f9534ee775b8">
<p local-id=3D"07da69b0af9a">How many eligible candidates and verified recr=
uiters are sufficient for the pilot; what zero-match rate and response rate=
 warrant scaling?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d380312e-c18c-4720-8bb9-782068150225">
<p local-id=3D"32c0d74e7921">Which specialist review and capacity sign-offs=
 permit recruiter-side activation at G2/G4, and which existing Should work =
is deferred if necessary?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e6dddbf-fcac-4673-85ae-080fd7d67e67">
<p local-id=3D"d25ec5425fbc">What recruiter quotas, cost ceiling and post-p=
ilot pricing model apply, independently of candidate credits and ranking?</=
p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"85484abd6c69" id=3D"CareerPilot=E2=80=93MVPPRD-Compatibilit=
yreview=E2=80=946October2026">Compatibility review =E2=80=94 6 October 2026=
</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1800" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"a=
2004714-8802-423b-8f2d-7a8e704c1442" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"e426c8f9-342b-450b-a795-6acf2825b69b">
<th data-local-id=3D"7e96446e-5926-46cb-9f72-f7257d465350" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"f6bf48127330">Finding</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"f9fc1cca-23f0-48c5-9a82-19a29dee43a1" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"d2ea60e50cc8">Resolution / remaining dependency</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"0ed82ad0-3514-4c77-b846-9d7807b5f63e">
<td data-local-id=3D"f952a44e-0268-4b0f-b1bc-e8079dc53abd" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f3102a32e19e">75% fit, 80% completeness and US3 50% explanat=
ion thresholds</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"35fb2046-845b-4e72-997c-75866dc53f51" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5ae265b92518">Updated fit band to 90% throughout; FR18 and r=
elated metrics/flow/questions to 90% completeness; US3 explanatory threshol=
d to 70%. These remain separate concepts.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"f442eb93-7a80-4841-b45c-710a06387241">
<td data-local-id=3D"e4d975a8-1f49-48a9-9988-aa99b19c7367" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"69c6a201cc07">Candidate-only MVP vs new headhunter service</=
p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c459c535-5660-4ac8-bd78-927f09507ec7" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"20b145150929">NFR9 and Out of Scope now distinguish an invit=
ation-only controlled pilot from broad post-launch employer access. No gene=
ral recruiter database access is granted.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"dced74b0-7676-4e00-a842-190bc7a9679f">
<td data-local-id=3D"1c7602af-006f-491c-8cc7-0045581b6b7a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c1893a248f1d">=E2=80=9CAll personas=E2=80=9D and single cand=
idate journey</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"1547c95a-1195-4236-b46b-84cab008c0d5" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1354881a8546">Existing =E2=80=9CAll=E2=80=9D means the three=
 candidate personas; added Sofia=E2=80=99s distinct use cases, goal and jou=
rney.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"98c31fe8-b909-41d0-bb88-f5de5498c1d1">
<td data-local-id=3D"fb9c0ca8-e3ac-4197-8d7c-12eb51eeebd9" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7de2227b5372">Existing lower-score journey examples (68%, 82=
%)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"ac68952e-6bed-4a25-9784-f861f82beeb0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c1a0a4e673eb">Retained as explicit individual evaluations or=
 optional near misses. They are not headhunter shortlist recommendations.</=
p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ac326756-d859-4043-ba7b-b1895b7877c9">
<td data-local-id=3D"30fc4327-14ec-49dc-88a7-b8582c3d54c2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6fbdab9dd1e0">Prepare credit unlocks full candidate evidence=
</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"a808ff4c-44c4-4b0f-835b-9cc64d77b46d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"105345af6f60">Candidate pricing remains; permitted headhunte=
r evidence is part of FR29 pilot review without charging the candidate.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"5a475b2c-4826-4bb7-9350-a6a922af2da4">
<td data-local-id=3D"b5b39356-df4b-46f7-816b-15e8058f4b21" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"761218457106">FR20 confidence is Should; pilot requires trus=
ted shortlists</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c56c14cf-aebc-482e-bbeb-cb24d4502118" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"523bf721e1fe">High confidence is mandatory for FR29 pilot el=
igibility even if the general candidate confidence feature remains Should.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"d525c6fc-9e67-43d8-88e2-fa6307625415">
<td data-local-id=3D"d2d64d19-331c-433b-841d-05ad1bc939e3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8f03273e1b56">FR14 / US13 stays post-MVP</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"64cd0c89-35c1-4641-bf09-9ab9b951b6cb" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"bd88569b95f5">Retained broad trust indicator scope; basic pi=
lot verification and report/block controls are separate prerequisites.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ba13f712-222d-4f2d-a899-52690db32ca0">
<td data-local-id=3D"607d3654-7880-4aec-9661-8886b40fff41" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"12ceb3f45ae3">Same fixed date/team with additional Must work=
</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"cf4b7811-5008-46ce-9167-e0c0bc639308" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"36a5e301d6e0">Pilot Musts are conditional on an estimated ca=
pacity plan and release gates. Existing sprint assignments remain; candidat=
e launch remains fixed. Pilot access stays disabled if gates fail.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"36e0f294-444b-42a4-bce8-f5a2390002e5">
<td data-local-id=3D"523f458f-9b29-4592-aaaf-b0da4e1a7a9c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d52b2809bb90">No automatic candidate data sharing or applica=
tion-history side effects</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"144d90c4-8f43-46af-a406-0a6f515acdf2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5d312f79fd04">Off-by-default opt-in, scoped candidate approv=
al, fresh availability and revocation required. Recruiter request history i=
s separate from FR11.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"aa286937-85e6-4cf0-a92f-e950ae1d2d3e">
<td data-local-id=3D"9c780990-5a5a-431a-b84f-94fe6f71a2ee" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6482ee699e88">Metrics and score gaming</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"f67abe63-df09-476c-9336-8391310eac3d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"74a2322af998">First seven metric targets tightened; final th=
ree unchanged. Add supply, expert precision, zero-match and cohort views so=
 strict filtering or inflated scores cannot masquerade as better fit.</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"150cba10-6845-41b2-9aff-1c8a080e59c7">
<td data-local-id=3D"1f0cf8c1-9b96-4426-94be-3b0522e63d06" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"215212979ef1">Existing issues outside this requested change<=
/p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"496a5426-2fbe-4bdb-a9e3-3c0c73935568" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ae29893e95e2">Jira contains duplicate unused build sprint se=
ries; S15 Beta text mentions Spain while PRD MVP remains Germany. Flag for =
planning cleanup; no unrelated sprint edits made.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"742109b2-114c-465e-800d-78e68f23e766">
<td data-local-id=3D"d61e8771-b88c-43ef-8f61-8b45e21dc866" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ac53c675775b">Remaining product decisions</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"867084af-778d-4b07-90d1-4d414e2f4bce" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9f8cebc49605">Verification evidence/owner, profile-preview f=
ields, seven-day freshness and access expiry, recipient retention, high-con=
fidence definition, pilot quotas/pricing and capacity sign-off remain open.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"e56b5d943458">
<td data-local-id=3D"b98d422ad2a9" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0bbf78cfc2ce">90% completeness gate (7 October 2026)</p></td=
>
<td data-local-id=3D"8417262e8cbb" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ad0a98aa788c">Removed for candidate matching: scores are alw=
ays shown with a confidence label, every list shows at least 10 jobs, and c=
ompleteness drives confidence and prompts (FR18, FR20). Headhunter shortlis=
t eligibility (FR29) still requires =E2=89=A590% completeness until the tea=
m decides otherwise.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"40c38f6b9eac">Existing FR1=E2=80=93FR24, NFR1=E2=80=93NFR11 =
and US1=E2=80=93US22 identifiers remain; new IDs continue as FR25=E2=80=93F=
R31, NFR12=E2=80=93NFR14 and US23=E2=80=93US29. Existing candidate hierarch=
y, application behaviour, 10-credit model, Germany/DE/EN constraints and la=
unch date are preserved except the explicitly revised thresholds and necess=
ary pilot access clarifications.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"544ab5f4c7e6" id=3D"CareerPilot=E2=80=93MVPPRD-12.LegalandC=
omplianceConsiderationsforaRealPilot">12. Legal and Compliance Consideratio=
ns for a Real Pilot</h2>
<p local-id=3D"895d4d4880f3"><strong>Scope. </strong>CareerPilot is a class=
room demo: it uses mock or clearly labelled job data, no real candidates, a=
nd stores no personal data. This chapter lists what would have to be in pla=
ce before a real pilot with real users in Germany; it does not describe the=
 demo, and it is not legal advice.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1800" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"3=
e5c6d340dc4" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"02e1a59f40f8">
<th data-local-id=3D"f75bf60ebec1" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"2dd8456cb5e6">Area</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"ea9e9986c4b2" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"2f79e773fd4d">What a real pilot needs</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"06dd825b028d" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"e281a952c96c">Related questions</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ca602f732e7d">
<td data-local-id=3D"0c0daf5de74f" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7d91de98a6f5">Data protection (GDPR, BDSG)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"7060b04473d9" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a59a998d0fe7">A legal basis for each use of data (account, m=
atching, documents). A data protection impact assessment, because the produ=
ct systematically evaluates people; that also makes a data protection offic=
er mandatory in Germany (=C2=A7 38 BDSG). Processing agreements with every =
processor (hosting, LLM, email), EU hosting or approved safeguards for non-=
EU providers, defined retention, and deletion that reaches CVs, generated d=
ocuments, logs and backups. Data export and deletion for users (NFR2).</p><=
/td>
<td data-local-id=3D"b3b62b2e1aa0" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5a01a68df56d">Q11</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"1ecaebb279ba">
<td data-local-id=3D"bbb0d5843066" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a3b6a65f4bce">Sensitive data in CVs</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"3673615d8619" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"97ab750ffb71">CVs often contain a photo, date of birth, nati=
onality and sometimes religion or health details. Minimise them at upload a=
nd never use them for scoring; special categories (GDPR Art. 9) are strippe=
d or need explicit consent.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"24cda60157db" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"39cebebe14bf">Q6, matching model</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"88dceaf46b27">
<td data-local-id=3D"c755fd3eaa45" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e121e40ef352">Automated decisions (GDPR Art. 22)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c7404f2ca92e" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7798e274f959">The candidate always decides whether to apply,=
 so no decision is fully automated. Any recruiter-side ranking needs a huma=
n in the loop and a way to contest it.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"980a2f336b50" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"22221dd26eba">=E2=80=94</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"cf0bd186a3c4">
<td data-local-id=3D"264d75f0cb0a" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e965fd03d70c">EU AI Act</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"3980478126a4" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d6954b895f6f">Specialist classification. Recruitment and sel=
ection AI is high-risk (Annex III), applicable from 2 December 2027 under t=
he current framework; a candidate-side assistant may fall outside it depend=
ing on intended purpose, recruiter-side evaluation clearly falls inside. Re=
gardless: disclose AI use, label AI-generated documents, keep scoring expla=
inable and traceable, monitor bias, and train the team in AI literacy.</p><=
/td>
<td data-local-id=3D"47f5fff383bc" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"dc83454ed8a4">Q10, HH 7</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"1f03289ec2a3">
<td data-local-id=3D"eb006435d5f0" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8933258ffcf4">Anti-discrimination (AGG)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"20cd2df4a638" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c174a4d5c4e1">No protected attributes or proxies in scoring.=
 Bias testing before launch and periodically with the four-fifths impact-ra=
tio method, and documented fixes when a gap is found.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"17f3b6a2e186" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"758c10ac0a0d">HH 5</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"b3e0faf93ecf">
<td data-local-id=3D"10fb638e547b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"3d3c2a8f24f2">Job data sources</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"b2fba375e652" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0259a20cd0b3">Terms of use for the Bundesagentur job lists; =
no scraping (database rights and site terms). Employer-posted jobs first, t=
hen licensed or contracted partner feeds. Mock data labelled as such.</p></=
td>
<td data-local-id=3D"8dc51b469f3c" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a6762d1134d6">Q9</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"2d2050b731c0">
<td data-local-id=3D"238c9a1e9675" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6c6b260c36f8">Payments and the wallet</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"29488abf3308" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"2572e78c03da">A wallet holding customer money can count as e=
-money, so it would run through a licensed provider rather than CareerPilot=
 holding funds; alternatively credits are sold as a prepaid digital service=
. Prices including VAT, consumer withdrawal rules for digital content, clea=
r terms.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"cbfee612a718" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5b882b0dc9da">Q1</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"66f2afc2e43e">
<td data-local-id=3D"ff9e84a76c83" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"939063e0b2f2">Recruiter pilot</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"07dc0aa04e82" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9eb76595cf5a">Organisation verification (commercial register=
 entry, domain, VAT ID) with a named approver and periodic rechecks. Pseudo=
nymised preview limited to agreed fields; purpose-bound, time-limited CV ac=
cess; recipient obligations in the recruiter terms; a report and suspension=
 process.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"96f981966f23" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"96c0117e423b">HH 1, 2, 4, 8</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"c4cd79eacefe">
<td data-local-id=3D"7f3530f160d4" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"91d0cb90619a">Website and platform duties</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"9e69e9db5850" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f157040c2f36">Imprint (Impressum), cookie consent, privacy n=
otice and the ranking-policy disclosure. The Accessibility Strengthening Ac=
t (BFSG) is likely relevant once consumers can buy credits.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"dcfb4a2dfb1d" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"74690f95ed77">NFR6, NFR10</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"520ca8e24b22">
<td data-local-id=3D"f11c55c1a67b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1982d37fa43c">Security</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"7152e079190a" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f0ebf30d46b0">Encryption in transit and at rest, role-based =
